    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317">

                <pb facs="0861" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1946v04/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.014/8–3046</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the Italian Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">di Stefano</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Deputy
                        Director of the Office of Near Eastern and African Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Villard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-30">August 30, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Villard</hi>: Following to our
                    conversations, I am enclosing herewith a short memorandum outlining the
                    amendments which, in view of the Italian Government, should be adopted in the
                    Italian peace treaty draft.</p>
                <p>The Italian Government would appreciate it very much if the State Department
                    could give them the most favorable consideration.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d317-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Thanking you again for your constant assistance, I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ario</hi>] <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >di Stefano</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d317-a1.xml" xpointer="d317-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d317-f1" n="38" xml:id="d317-f1-content">
                <p>In a memorandum dated September 18, the Department of State acknowledged the
                    receipt of the Italian memorandum and indicated that it had been transmitted to
                    the United States Delegation in Paris for appropriate action
                    (865.014/8–3046).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
